- **CI contracts:** `wpt_diff_to_pr.py` consumes `wpt diff --format json` entries with `test`, `kind`, `status`, `counts`, `before`, `after`, `counts_before`, `counts_after` (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:2; .github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:34-52); PR section delimited by `<!-- wpt-results-start -->` / `<!-- wpt-results-end -->`, replaced on re-runs (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:4-5; .github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:14-15; .github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:252-260); CLI `diff_file`, `--repo`, `--pr`, `--run-url`, `--areas`, `--dry-run` (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:274-280), `--areas` naming the per-area subtest changes that upstream's `.github/scripts/wpt_area_changes.py` computes from the two reports (.github/scripts/wpt_area_changes.py:1-92); "PASS" and "OK" pass, listing capped at 400 lines (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:17-19; .github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:231-239); appends to `GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` and PATCHes the PR body through `gh api` (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:293-308); WPT artifacts `wpt-report.json.zst` and `wpt-diff` (.github/workflows/wpt.yml:52-56; .github/workflows/wpt.yml:80-87; .github/workflows/wpt-post-results.yml:22-27); `repository-dispatch` `update-results` to `DioxusLabs/blitz-wpt-results` after WPT on main, only when `github.repository == 'DioxusLabs/blitz'` (.github/workflows/wpt.yml:101-113; .github/workflows/wpt.yml:103); `.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh {leg}` — legs `fmt` · `clippy` (the workspace line, then, only when green and since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, upstream's own `cargo clippy -p blitz-dom --no-default-features --features svg,woff,accessibility,system-fonts,file-input,custom-widget --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`;
 .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:21-25) · `test` · `ci-scripts` · `build` · `msrv` (`cargo +1.91 build`) · `counter` · `wasm` · `doc` (`cargo doc --workspace --no-deps`) · `audit` (`cargo deny --locked --workspace --all-features check advisories licenses`, the whole workspace's graph, since 2026-10-14-quality-gates; `cargo deny check advisories` until then) · `a11y` (the `accessibility_hidden`, `accessibility_roles`, `focusability_updates`, `stand_keyboard`, `stand_contrast` and `stand_accessibility_ids` integration tests — six since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions, three until then, widened on the founder's F4 «Расширить задание a11y (Рекомендую)» with no new job, no required status check and no `ci.yml` change, its pin `LegScriptTest.test_gate_legs_dispatch_to_cargo_and_write_their_log`; .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:39; .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:298-299) · `coverage` (`cargo llvm-cov` lcov to `target/coverage/lcov.info`, then its per-file report, then, chained since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, `python3 .github/scripts/coverage_floor.py` over three crate floors, the leg exiting with the floor's status; since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync both `cargo llvm-cov` lines take `--ignore-filename-regex 'keyboard_compat\.rs$'`, excluding dioxus-native-dom's crate-private `keyboard_compat.rs`, upstream's temporary keyboard-types 0.7/0.8 bridge, until escher takes upstream's retirement of it — `coverage_floor.py` and the three floors unchanged — pinned by `test_coverage_leg_reaches_the_floor_on_each_crate` (.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:41-42; .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:44-45;
 .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:327)) · `stand-repeat` (since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, not a fast leg: three rounds, each printing `stand-repeat: round R of 3` and running `cargo test -p blitz-tests --locked` with one `--test` per `tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_*.rs`, then `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked` over `cli_commands`, `cli_flow`, `host_binary`, `host_log`, `host_timer`, `mcp_server`, `mcp_log` and `recording`; the first red command ends the leg with its status — a zero-failure budget, no retry, no `--ignored`, no env var — and three green rounds end `stand-repeat: 3 of 3 rounds green`; the script reads the floor script and the `stand_*.rs` set beside itself, `SCRIPTS="$(dirname "$0")"`; .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:48-65) · `fast` (fmt → clippy → test → ci-scripts, stopping at the first red: the local pre-push gate), every cargo leg `--locked` but `examples/wasm_hello` (no `Cargo.lock`); it tees the leg's merged output to `target/ci-logs/{leg}.log`, truncated at the leg's start, exits with the leg command's status, and prints the leg list to stderr and exits 2 on an unknown or missing leg (.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:8-89); every ci.yml leg job ends with `actions/upload-artifact` (SHA-pinned, `# v7`) `if: failure()` named `ci-log-{job id}` (matrix `ci-log-matrix-{platform}`), uploading only its own log under `target/ci-logs/`, `retention-days: 7`, `if-no-files-found: ignore` (.github/workflows/ci.yml:48-54; .github/workflows/ci.yml:419-425); the `coverage` job alone also uploads `coverage-report` — `target/coverage/`, `if: success()`, `retention-days: 7` — the one fork-CI artifact outside `target/ci-logs/` (.github/workflows/ci.yml:286-291); the contract is pinned by `test_ci_workflows.py` (.github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:103-496);
 the package-install contract `bash .github/scripts/apt-install.sh [--attempts N] [--bound SECONDS] [--pause SECONDS] <package>...`, the one statement of fork CI's package install: up to 3 attempts, each `sudo timeout --kill-after=10 120 apt-get update` and then `apt-get install -y <packages>` under the same bound; a failed call — the bound's expiry included — prints one stderr line `apt-install: attempt {n} of {N} failed in {repair|update|install} (exit {status})`, pauses 10 s when another attempt remains, and the next attempt starts, since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, with a bounded repair — `sudo timeout --kill-after=10 120 dpkg --configure -a`, phase `repair`, a failed repair failing that attempt — and then `update`, the first attempt running no `dpkg` (the operator's answer «Add a bounded repair» at that chunk's P4); exit grammar `0` an attempt completed · `1` every attempt failed · `2` usage — never the bound's own 124 or 137; its arguments are checked before any command runs — a package name must match `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9+.-]+$`, an option value `^(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,5})$`, `--attempts` and `--bound` are at least 1, and at least one package is named; four constants at its head (`ATTEMPTS=3`, `BOUND=120`, `PAUSE=10`, and the kill grace `GRACE=10`, which no option sets), no environment variable of its own and no file written; ten `run:` steps of ci.yml call it (nine until 2026-10-14-quality-gates) with package names and no option, no leg of `ci-leg.sh` calls it and the dev host never runs it against a package manager; a bound that fires inside `apt-get install` can leave dpkg interrupted, which the next attempt's repair configures — no run has shown it on a real interrupted dpkg, the stand-in tests its one witness;
 it is pinned by `InstallScriptTest`, eight tests (five until 2026-10-14-quality-gates) that run it against a stand-in `sudo`, `apt-get` and `dpkg` with the real `timeout`, and by the workflow invariant `test_o_package_installs_are_bounded`, both in the `ci-scripts` leg (.github/scripts/apt-install.sh:17-73; .github/scripts/apt-install.sh:52-60; .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:218-235; .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:378-492) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-09-audit-corrections-agent-surfaces/report.md, the repair at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-quality-gates/report.md; the coverage-floor contract `python3 .github/scripts/coverage_floor.py LCOV CRATE_DIR=PERCENT …` (stdlib, since 2026-10-14-quality-gates): it sums `LF`/`LH` over every `SF` record whose real path, relative to the working directory, lies under each crate directory, prints one line per crate, `{dir} {hit}/{lines} = {pct:.2f} % (floor {f} %)`, then `coverage floor: N of N crates at or above their floors` (exit 0) or `coverage floor: K of N crates under their floors` (exit 1); a crate with no record exits 2 naming its directory on stderr and a malformed argument exits 2 with a usage line; it prints no source path but the crate directory and never echoes the lcov path; the `coverage` leg calls it with `packages/escher-driver=97 packages/dioxus-native-dom=83 packages/blitz-test-harness=90`; pinned by `test_coverage_floor.py` (`CoverageFloorTest`, 7 cases) and two `LegScriptTest` cases, in the `ci-scripts` leg (.github/scripts/coverage_floor.py:70-101; .github/scripts/test_coverage_floor.py:17-88);
 the agent-run test contract `bash scripts/agent-run.sh {boot | run {stand|all|name} | status | cleanup | logs}`, run from the repository root, drives `cargo test -p blitz-tests --locked` with exit grammar `0` success · `1` failed (an empty run included) · `2` usage, checked before · `3` precondition unmet, JSON-line events (`boot`, `run.start`, `test`, `run.end`, `status`, `cleanup`) encoded by an embedded python3 `json`, and state in `target/agent-run/` only — full contract in test-plan §3; `scripts/agent-run.ps1` is a pass-through Windows entry with no logic; pinned by `test_agent_run.py`, run by the existing `ci-scripts` leg (scripts/agent-run.sh:1-226; scripts/agent-run.ps1:1-4; .github/scripts/test_agent_run.py:88-266); the cold-agent run pipe `bash scripts/cold-agent.sh {run <task> | status | cleanup | logs}`, run from the repository root with the one task `stand` (since 2026-10-15-cold-agent-test; `counter` retired), follows the same grammar — exit `0` success · `1` a `failed` verdict · `2` usage, checked before any precondition · `3` precondition unmet (`claude` or `python3` not on PATH, `target/debug/escher-session` absent or not executable — one stderr line naming `cargo build --locked -p seven_guis --bin escher-session`, the pipe building nothing — no verdict, no `events.jsonl`) — with JSON-line events (`run.start`, `run.end`, `status`, `cleanup`) encoded by an embedded python3 `json` and state in `target/cold-agent/` only; `run` starts one isolated `claude -p` session (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-06) from a per-run `mktemp -d` directory with the fixed prompt `STAND_PROMPT` and only the escher server's twelve tools
 — the driver's own `escher-session mcp` (`--tools ""`, `--strict-mcp-config`, `--allowedTools mcp__escher`, `--setting-sources ""`, `--disable-slash-commands`, `--no-session-persistence`, `--model claude-opus-5-5`, `--max-budget-usd 3`, under `timeout 600`) — and writes `verdict.json` — `passed` only on positive evidence (client exit 0, a successful `result`, isolated — the twelve `mcp__escher__{verb}` tools, one server `escher` connected —, `counts_agree` between the server's `tool_call` span lines and the transcript, at least one tool call, all four lean apps met from the tool's own `snapshot` answers, and the agent's last fenced JSON check (≤ 65,536 bytes, ≤ 400 steps, closed keys and verbs) replayed passing on a fresh `escher-session mcp` child and failing on an ablated replay on a second), `wrong_calls` recorded and deciding nothing; the stub `scripts/cold_agent_stub.py` was deleted at 2026-10-15-cold-agent-test; `scripts/cold-agent.ps1` is a pass-through; pinned by `test_cold_agent.py` (a `claude` shim and a fake `escher-session`; no live model, credential or built binary), run by the existing `ci-scripts` leg — full contract in test-plan §3 (scripts/cold-agent.sh:13-29; scripts/cold-agent.sh:148-308; scripts/cold-agent.sh:450-482; .github/scripts/test_cold_agent.py:67-128; .github/scripts/test_cold_agent.py:200-222); the blitz-tests target contract — `[package]` does not set `autotests` to false, and the manifest holds exactly one `[[test]]` table, `all` at `tests/all.rs` with `test = false` — pinned by `test_blitz_tests_targets.py` (`BlitzTestsTargetsTest`, one test), run by the same leg, which discovers seven test files since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, six until then (.github/scripts/test_blitz_tests_targets.py:17-26; tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:56-59);
 root crate feature `log-times` = `log-frame-times` + `log-phase-times` forwarding to dioxus-native (Cargo.toml:265-268)
